<h2>14. Enterprise / Cloud Deployment</h2>

<h3>Scaling to 100,000+ Pages</h3>
<p>The endpoint audits one URL per call, so scale comes from your client:</p>
<ul>
<li>Run a bounded worker pool. Process URLs with a fixed number of concurrent calls, and back off on HTTP 429.</li>
<li>Read the sitemap yourself. Parse your sitemap (and any sitemap index files) into a URL list, as in the sitemap example. <code>POST /v1/intel/sitemap</code> can also fetch and parse one for you.</li>
<li>Schedule incremental audits. Run a full audit monthly and incremental audits weekly for pages changed in the last 7 days.</li>
<li>Store your own results. Keep each run's scores in your database so you can trend them and diff runs.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Multi-Tenant Usage</h3>
<p>For agencies managing multiple client sites, create a separate API key per client (<code>POST /v1/keys</code> accepts a <code>label</code>, a <code>project_tag</code>, and an optional <code>daily_cap_credits</code>). Each client's calls then show up separately in your usage history, and a runaway job cannot spend past its cap.</p>

<h3>Observability</h3>
<p><code>GET /v1/me/usage</code> and <code>GET /v1/me/usage/summary</code> return your call history and totals. Trend lines such as average score over time come from the results you store.</p>

